tent":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"duration_ms\":33803,\"duration_api_ms\":33803,\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"Gathering issue details, repo context, and action SHAs for the CI workflow.\\n\\n\\n## Completion\\n\\n**Commit:** `6caf5efc1f3bb15f0b62a6ba6c8bc121b3e990b0`\\n\\n**Pinned actions:**\\n| Action | SHA | Tag |\\n|--------|-----|-----|\\n| `actions/checkout` | `fbc6f3992d24b796d5a048ff273f7fcc4a7b6c09` | v5 |\\n| `dtolnay/rust-toolchain` | `6bed0761d98439e5a578e2877258200ad565ba87` | stable |\\n| `Swatinem/rust-cache` | `6323deb102c322ba6fcbdcafc7e3dddab59af2b6` | v2.9.2 |\\n\\n**Local checks:** `cargo fmt --check` — exit 0; `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` — exit 0 (clean build ~5s).\\n\\n**Friction:**\\n- Issue #8 still lists blocked-by #6 (recording script); the brief overrode that, but the issue metadata is stale.\\n- `dtolnay/rust-toolchain` has no `vX` tag on the resolved ref; used `# stable` per the lookup instruction while the pin format example only showed versioned actions.\\n- No [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/claude/review-19.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":9,"content":"{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"commands_changed\",\"commands\":[{\"name\":\"autonomous-flywheel\",\"description\":\"Flywheel unattended multi-PR landing: implement, triage CI, merge on green, morning report. Fires when asked to land a stack of PRs unattended or continue a flywheel session. (user)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"clear-communication\",\"description\":\"Write and edit prose in GOV.UK / GDS style — plain English, active voice, front-loaded, sentence case, no bold/italic emphasis. Use when writing or editing reports, research write-ups, guidance, documentation, summaries, or any prose where clarity and accessibility matter. (user)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"code-review\",\"description\":\"Review the changes since a fixed point (commit, branch, tag, or merge-base) along two axes: Standards (does the code follow this repo's documented coding standards?) and Spec (does the code match what the originating issue/spec asked for?). Runs both reviews in parallel sub-agents and reports them side by side. [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":16,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01CtvwRn678gy36PGvnifeBK\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"title:\\tci: Linux workflow (fmt, clippy, tests) (#8)\\nstate:\\tDRAFT\\nauthor:\\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\\nlabels:\\t\\nassignees:\\t\\nreviewers:\\t\\nprojects:\\t\\nmilestone:\\t\\nnumber:\\t19\\nurl:\\thttps://github.com/user/delegate/pull/19\\nadditions:\\t23\\ndeletions:\\t0\\nauto-merge:\\tdisabled\\n--\\nFixes #8\\n\\nOne `ci` job on `ubuntu-latest` for pull requests and pushes to `main`: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test`. Ignored live tests stay excluded. Every action is pinned by SHA, the token is read-only, and `pull_request_target` is not used.\\n\\nImplemented by composer-2.5 via `scripts/record.sh` (fixture lands with #18).\\n\\nCo-authored with Claude Code.\\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\\nnew file mode 100644\\nindex 0000000..ede11d5\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\\n@@ -0,0 +1,23 @ [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":23,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"Exit code 1\\nAGENTS.md\\nbin\\nCargo.lock\\nCargo.toml\\nCODE-REVIEW.md\\nconfig\\ndocs\\nLICENSE\\nparity\\nREADME.md\\nskills\\nspec.md\\nsrc\\ntarget\\ntests\\nworkflows\\n(eval):1: no matches found: rust-toolchain*\\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.rs\\nfbc6f3992d24b796d5a048ff273f7fcc4a7b6c09\\n6bed0761d98439e5a578e2877258200ad565ba87\\n6323deb1