=N` records a run cancelled with SIGTERM.\\n- `scripts/redact.jq` strips the recording user's setup (pi system-prompt sections and extension tool schemas; Claude init lists and hook output). The home-directory name is replaced with `user`.\\n- 22 recorded runs across cursor, pi and Claude: plain answer, tool calls, r [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/claude/plan-plain-answer.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":9,"content":"{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"commands_changed\",\"commands\":[{\"name\":\"autonomous-flywheel\",\"description\":\"Flywheel unattended multi-PR landing: implement, triage CI, merge on green, morning report. Fires when asked to land a stack of PRs unattended or continue a flywheel session. (user)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"clear-communication\",\"description\":\"Write and edit prose in GOV.UK / GDS style — plain English, active voice, front-loaded, sentence case, no bold/italic emphasis. Use when writing or editing reports, research write-ups, guidance, documentation, summaries, or any prose where clarity and accessibility matter. (user)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"code-review\",\"description\":\"Review the changes since a fixed point (commit, branch, tag, or merge-base) along two axes: Standards (does the code follow this repo's documented coding standards?) and Spec (does the code match what the originating issue/spec asked for?). Runs both reviews in parallel sub-agents and reports them side by side. [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/claude/error-bad-model.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":10,"content":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"diagnostics\":null,\"id\":\"ffbfddb0-f223-4657-9613-601878cbfb75\",\"container\":null,\"model\":\"<synthetic>\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"stop_details\":null,\"stop_reason\":\"stop_sequence\",\"stop_sequence\":\"\",\"type\":\"message\",\"usage\