{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**1. Contradictions**  \n- #15 is blocked by #13, but `__supervise` on origin/main still runs `JobRegistry`; #13 says the supervisor must not use it — **implement #13 supervisor first, then split backends.**  \n- #15 puts doctor on each backend; #11 owns `delegate doctor` — **backend exposes probe hooks only; CLI stays in #11.**  \n- #15 asks for a normalized parser result; finalize still uses `RawCursorJson` and `output.rs` STATUS parsing (#7) — **keep `BackendResult`; do not move STATUS derivation into the backend.**  \n- `cli.rs` calls `build_argv`, `map_capability`, and `cursor_bin` — violates the encapsulation AC — **move argv, capability flags, and bin resolution into `backends/cursor`.**  \n- `capability.rs` still maps removed Plan/Write modes — **delete non-spec capabilities in the same lane or cursor backend ignores them.**\n\n**2. Unstated defaults**  \n- Shape of the backend trait (`run` only vs `build_argv` / `resume_session` / doctor probes) — **trait: `resolve_bin`, `build_argv`, `run`; resume argv helper; doctor as associated fns.**  \n- Location of `stream.rs` — **leave at crate root for #17 claude reuse; cursor backend owns the only caller for now.**  \n- Fixture coverage — **test every `tests/fixtures/cursor/*.stdout` on main except argv/stderr-only peers.**  \n- Backend dispatch — **hardcode cursor models until #16/#17; stub `backend not implemented` matches #11.**\n\n**3. Failure behaviour gaps**  \n- Cancelled runs: no `result` line (#6) — **parser may be partial; supervisor alone sets CANCELLED.**  \n- Cursor bad model: empty stdout, message on stderr, exit 1 — **treat as error from exit + stderr, not stream JSON.**  \n- Truncated NDJSON — **skip unparseable lines; error only if no terminal result when exit is clean.**\n\n**4. Acceptance criteria conflicts**  \n- “Nothing outside cursor knows stream format” vs global `stream` module and `RawCursorJson` — **hide types behind `backends/cursor`; pub use only `Backend` trait at boundary.**  \n- “Fixture parser tests” vs inline JSON in `stream.rs` tests — **add fixture tests; keep inline smoke tests.**  \n- “All tests unchanged” vs moving `build_argv` — **behaviour unchanged; runner unit tests may import cursor backend instead of `runner::build_argv`.**\n\n**Fixtures vs #15 cursor parser**  \nCursor must stay on NDJSON `type:result` + `thinking`/`tool_call`, session on the result line, errors often stdout-empty (#6). Do not copy pi’s `agent_end`/`stopReason` or exit-0 errors, or claude’s hooks, `total_cost_usd`, or `permission_denials` — those belong in #16/#17. STATUS-line text in `needs-context` fixtures is shared; cursor still delivers raw result text to `output.rs`.\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS"}]},"session_id":"7dd612d0-6469-4d8d-870b-f50c14f3831a"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":74677,"duration_api_ms":74677,"is_error":false,"result":"Gathering issues, spec comments, owner rulings, and relevant code on origin/main.\n\n\n**1. Contradictions**  \n- #15 is blocked by #13, but `__supervise` on origin/main still runs `JobRegistry`; #13 says the supervisor must not use it — **implement #13 supervisor first, then split backends.**  \n- #15 puts doctor on each backend; #11 owns `delegate doctor` — **backend exposes probe hooks only; CLI stays in #11.**  \n- #15 asks for a normalized parser result; finalize still uses `RawCursorJson` and `output.rs` STATUS parsing (#7) — **keep `BackendResult`; do not move STATUS derivation into the backend.**  \n- `cli.rs` calls `build_argv`, `map_capability`, and `cursor_bin` — violates the encapsulation AC — **move argv, capability flags, and bin resolution into `backends/cursor`.**  \n- `capability.rs` still maps removed Plan/Write modes — **delete non-spec capabilities in the same lane or cursor backend ignores them.**\n\n**2. Unstated defaults**  \n- Shape of the backend trait (`run` only vs `build_argv` / `resume_session` / doctor probes) — **trait: `resolve_bin`, `build_argv`, `run`; resume argv helper; doctor as associated fns.**  \n- Location of `stream.rs` — **leave at crate root for #17 claude reuse; cursor backend owns the only caller for now.**  \n- Fixture coverage — **test every `tests/fixtures/cursor/*.stdout` on main except argv/stderr-only peers.**  \n- Backend dispatch — **hardcode cursor models until #16/#17; stub `backend not implemented` matches #11.**\n\n**3. Failure behaviour gaps**  \n- Cancelled runs: no `result` line (#6) — **parser may be partial; supervisor alone sets CANCELLED.**  \n- Cursor bad model: empty stdout, message on stderr, exit 1 — **treat as error from exit + stderr, not stream JSON.**  \n- Truncated NDJSON — **skip unparseable lines; error only if no terminal result when exit is clean.**\n\n**4. Acceptance criteria conflicts**  \n- “Nothing outside cursor knows stream format” vs global `stream` module and `RawCursorJson` — **hide types behind `backends/cursor`; pub use only `Backend` trait at boundary.**  \n- “Fixture parser tests” vs inline JSON in `stream.rs` tests — **add fixture tests; keep inline smoke tests.**  \n- “All tests unchanged” vs moving `build_argv` — **behaviour unchanged; runner unit tests may import cursor backend instead of `runner::build_argv`.**\n\n**Fixtures vs #15 cursor parser**  \nCursor must stay on NDJSON `type:result` + `thinking`/`tool_call`, session on the result line, errors often stdout-empty (#6). Do not copy pi’s `agent_end`/`stopReason` or exit-0 errors, or claude’s hooks, `total_cost_usd`, or `permission_denials` — those belong in #16/#17. STATUS-line text in `needs-context` fixtures is shared; cursor still delivers raw result text to `output.rs`.\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS","session_id":"7dd612d0-6469-4d8d-870b-f50c14f3831a","request_id":"13e7813c-8061-40d0-a475-19ebe85b4952","usage":{"inputTokens":48283,"outputTokens":5900,"cacheReadTokens":519712,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
